 2027 second quarter', 'value': '$59.7 billion', 'kind': 'actual', 'basis': None, 'party': 'NVIDIA'}, {'n': 6, 'measure': 'Net income growth year over year', 'period': 'fiscal 2027 second quarter', 'value': '126%', 'kind': 'actual', 'basis': None, 'party': 'NVIDIA'}] LINKS none\nSTATEMENT e2 PARTY NVIDIA DATE None PASSAGES ['Guidance for the fiscal third quarter is $108 billion in revenue , around 12% above fiscal Q2.'] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'Revenue guidance', 'period': 'fiscal third quarter', 'value': '$108 billion', 'kind': 'guidance', 'basis': None, 'party': 'NVIDIA'}, {'n': 2, 'measure': 'Guidance growth versus fiscal Q2 revenue', 'period': 'fiscal third quarter', 'value': 'around 12%', 'kind': 'guidance', 'basis': 'sequential, versus fiscal Q2', 'party': 'NVIDIA'}] LINKS none\nSTATEMENT e3 PARTY NVIDIA (CFO Colette Kress) DATE late August 2026 PASSAGES ['And on the company\\'s late-August earnings call, CFO Colette Kress said Nvidia expects revenue to rise roughly 70% in fiscal 2028, the year ending in January 2028. She called it \"a supply-constrained outlook.\"'] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'Revenue growth year over year', 'period': 'fiscal 2028 (year ending January 2028)', 'value': 'roughly 70%', 'kind': 'guidance', 'basis': 'described by the CFO as \"a supply-constrained outlook\"', 'party': 'NVIDIA (CFO Colette Kress)'}] LINKS [{'question': 'clean-2', 'new_question': False, 'reason': \"The CFO's statement that fiscal 2028 growth is limited by manufacturing capacity, not customer demand, bears on how much NVIDIA must commit to purchase and supply capacity for that growth; it does not itself quantify any purchase or supply commitment.\"}]\nSTATEMENT e4 PARTY NVIDIA (CFO Colette Kress) DATE late August 2026 PASSAGES [\"On the call, Kress said gross margins should bottom between 71% and 72% in the fiscal fourth quarter and then settle at 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as price hikes kick in. That'd be a drop from the fiscal second quarter's 75%, though a s