2', 'new_question': False, 'reason': \"Gives a figure for NVIDIA's supply commitments ($279 billion) that the thesis tracks against the purchase and supply commitment amount disclosed in the next Form 10-K; the item gives no as-of date, so it cannot be tied to a specific reporting period.\"}]\nSTATEMENT e8 PARTY 24/7 Wall St. DATE None PASSAGES ['Real risks include supply commitments of $279 billion, guarantee obligations capped at $108.5 billion, and DSO extending to 60 days.'] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'guarantee obligations (capped)', 'period': None, 'value': '$108.5 billion', 'kind': 'estimate', 'basis': 'capped; source and as-of date not stated in the item', 'party': '24/7 Wall St.'}] LINKS [{'question': 'clean-1', 'new_question': False, 'reason': \"States a $108.5 billion cap on NVIDIA's guarantee obligations, the exact quantity the thesis tracks at the next annual report; the item does not say whether this reflects disclosed guarantees, credit support for AI labs and cloud partners, or the analyst's own aggregation.\"}]\nSTATEMENT e9 PARTY 24/7 Wall St. DATE None PASSAGES ['Real risks include supply commitments of $279 billion, guarantee obligations capped at $108.5 billion, and DSO extending to 60 days.'] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'days sales outstanding (DSO)', 'period': None, 'value': '60 days', 'kind': 'estimate', 'basis': 'described as extending', 'party': '24/7 Wall St.'}] LINKS none\nSTATEMENT e13 PARTY NVIDIA DATE None PASSAGES ['Gross margins are expected to bottom in the 71% to 72% range in Q4 on memory cost inflation, recovering to 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as volumes scale.'] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'gross margin', 'period': 'Q4 fiscal 2027', 'value': '71% to 72%', 'kind': 'guidance', 'basis': 'expected to bottom, on memory cost inflation', 'party': 'NVIDIA'}, {'n': 2, 'measure': 'gross margin', 'period': 'fiscal 2028', 'value': '72% to 73%', 'kind': 'guidance', 'basis': 'recovery as volumes scale', 'party': 'NVIDIA'}] LINKS none\nANSWER B39 ARTICLE 6\nSTATEMENT ev-q2-fy27-results PARTY NVIDIA DATE None PASSAGES ['Q2 fiscal 2027 delivered revenue of $96.22 billion, up 105.85% year over year, with non-GAAP EPS of $2.22 beating consensus by 6.29%. Data Center revenue hit $89.023 billion.'] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'revenue', 'period': 'Q2 fiscal 2027', 'value': '$96.22 billion', 'kind': 'actual', 'basis': None, 'party': 'NVIDIA'}, {'n': 2, 'measure': 'revenue growth year over year', 'period': 'Q2 fiscal 2027', 'value': '105.85%', 'kind': 'actual', 'basis': 'year over year', 'party': 'NVIDIA'}, {'n': 3, 'measure': 'non-GAAP EPS', 'period': 'Q2 fiscal 2027', 'value': '$2.22', 'kind': 'actual', 'basis': 'non-GAAP', 'party': 'NVIDIA'}, {'n': 4, 'measure': 'Data Center revenue', 'period': 'Q2 fiscal 2027', 'value': '$89.023 billion', 'kind': 'actual', 'basis': 'Data Center', 'party': 'NVIDIA'}] LINKS none\nSTATEMENT ev-q3-fy27-guidance-china-exclusion PARTY NVIDIA DATE None PASSAGES ['Management guided Q3 to $108 billion.', 'Q3 guidance excludes China Data Center compute revenue citing geopolitical uncertainty.'] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'revenue guidance', 'period': 'Q3 fiscal 2027', 'value': '$108 billion', 'kind': 'guidance', 'basis': 'excludes China Data Center compute revenue', 'party': 'NVIDIA'}] LINKS [{'question': 'clean-3', 'new_question': False, 'reason': 'The guidance excludes China Data Center compute revenue, showing China data-center sales are not in the Q3 outlook and bearing on whether NVIDIA can resume China sales in FY2027.'}]\nSTATEMENT ev-gross-margin-guidance PARTY NVIDIA DATE None PASSAGES ['Gross margins are expected to bottom in the 71% to 72% range in Q4 on memory cost inflation, recovering to 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as volumes scale.'] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'gross margin', 'period': 'Q4', 'value': '71% to 72%', 'kind': 'guidance', 'basis': 'on memory cost inflation', 'party': 'NVIDIA'}, {'n': 2, 'measure': 'gross margin', 'period': 'fiscal 2028', 'value': '72% to 73%', 'kind': 'guidance', 'basis': 'as volumes scale', 'party': 'NVIDIA'}] LINKS none\nSTATEMENT ev-supply-guarantees-dso PARTY NVIDIA DATE None PASSAGES ['Real risks include supply commitments of $279 billion, guarantee obligations capped at $108.5 billion, and DSO extending to 60 days.'] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'supply commitments', 'period': None, 'value': '$279 billion', 'kind': 'actual', 'basis': None, 'party': 'NVIDIA'}, {'n': 2, 'measure': 'guarantee obligations', 'period': None, 'value': '$108.5 billion', 'kind': 'actual', 'basis': 'capped at', 'party': 'NVIDIA'}, {'n': 3, 'measure': 'days sales outstanding (DSO)', 'period': None, 'value': '60 days', 'kind': 'actual', 'basis': 'extending to', 'party': 'NVIDIA'}] LINKS [{'question': 'clean-2', 'new_question': False, 'reason': 'Reports $279 billion of supply commitments, directly the purchase/supply commitment amount clean-2 tracks at the next annual report.'}, {'question': 'clean-1', 'new_question': False, 'reason': 'Reports guarantee obligations capped at $108.5 billion, directly the credit-support/guarantee amount clean-1 tracks at the next annual report.'}]\nSTATEMENT ev-jensen-supply-demand-growth PARTY Jensen Huang DATE None PASSAGES ['Jensen Huang told investors NVIDIA can supply only 70% of demand, with fiscal 2028 growth pegged at approximately 70%.'] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'share of demand NVIDIA can supply', 'period': None, 'value': '70%', 'kind': 'estimate', 'basis': None, 'party': 'Jensen Huang'}, {'n': 2, 'measure': 'fiscal 2028 growth', 'period': 'fiscal 2028', 'value': 'approximately 70%', 'kind': 'guidance', 'basis': None, 'party': 'Jensen Huang'}] LINKS [{'question': 'clean-4', 'new_question': False, 'reason': \"The CEO's statement that NVIDIA can supply only 70% of demand and his ~70% fiscal 2028 growth forecast indicate demand exceeds supply, a demand signal for the Vera Rubin ramp; it does not confirm shipment timing.\"}]\nSTATEMENT ev-vera-rubin-platform-value PARTY 24/7 Wall St. DATE 2026-09-23 PASSAGES [\"Vera Rubin ramps platform value per gigawatt from Blackwell's $25 billion to $40 billion.\"] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'platform value per gigawatt (Blackwell)', 'period': None, 'value': '$25 billion', 'kind': 'estimate', 'basis': 'Blackwell', 'party': '24/7 Wall St.'}, {'n': 2, 'measure': 'platform value per gigawatt (Vera Rubin)', 'period': None, 'value': '$40 billion', 'kind': 'estimate', 'basis': 'Vera Rubin', 'party': '24/7 Wall St.'}] LINKS [{'question': 'clean-4', 'new_question': False, 'reason': \"Provides an estimate of Vera Rubin's platform value per gigawatt versus Blackwell, informing the economics of the Vera Rubin ramp tracked by the thesis; it does not establish shipment timing.\"}]\nANSWER B53 ARTICLE 2\nSTATEMENT ev-1 PARTY Nvidia DATE May PASSAGES ['In May, Nvidia told shareholders that it would increase its quarterly payout to $0.25 per share from $0.01 per share. That’s a 2,400% increase, according to my calculations!'] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'quarterly dividend per share', 'period': 'quarterly', 'value': '$0.25 per share', 'kind': 'actual', 'basis': None, 'party': 'Nvidia'}, {'n': 2, 'measure': 'prior quarterly dividend per share', 'period': 'quarterly', 'value': '$0.01 per share', 'kind': 'actual', 'basis': None, 'party': 'Nvidia'}, {'n': 3, 'measure': 'increase in quarterly dividend', 'period': None, 'value': '2,400%', 'kind': 'actual', 'basis': \"author's calculation\", 'party': 'Morningstar'}] LINKS none\nSTATEMENT ev-2 PARTY Nvidia DATE None PASSAGES ['Indeed, Nvidia announced an $80 billion share buyback program at the time of its dividend declaration.'] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'share buyback program', 'period': None, 'value': '$80 billion', 'kind': 'actual', 'basis': None, 'party': 'Nvidia'}] LINKS none\nSTATEMENT ev-3 PARTY Nvidia DATE None PASSAGES ['Lost in a torrent of news about Nvidia NVDA this year—its role in financing $500 billion in artificial intelligence investments , its forecasts of 70% year-on-year revenue growth , and its acquisition of Hugging Face —was a dividend announcement.', 'That doesn’t fit with the 70% revenue growth forecast.'] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'year-on-year revenue growth forecast', 'period': None, 'value': '70%', 'kind': 'guidance', 'basis': None, 'party': 'Nvidia'}] LINKS none\nSTATEMENT ev-4 PARTY Nvidia DATE None PASSAGES ['Lost in a torrent of news about Nvidia NVDA this year—its role in financing $500 billion in artificial intelligence investments , its forecasts of 70% year-on-year revenue growth , and its acquisition of Hugging Face —was a dividend announcement.'] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'artificial intelligence investments Nvidia has a role in financing', 'period': None, 'value': '$500 billion', 'kind': 'actual', 'basis': 'as described by the article; no split between guarantees, credit support and equity investment', 'party': None}] LINKS [{'question': 'clean-1', 'new_question': False, 'reason': \"Indicates the scale of Nvidia's financial involvement in AI investments ($500 billion) that the annual-report disclosure of guarantees, credit-support commitments and revenue backstops would quantify; the article does not separate guarantees or credit support from equity investment, so it speaks to magnitude only.\"}]\nANSWER B59 ARTICLE 8\nSTATEMENT ev-1 PARTY Nvidia DATE None PASSAGES [\"Nvidia's latest results make the growth requirement seem nearly routine. Revenue in the fiscal 2027 second quarter (the period ended July 26, 2026) came to $96.2 billion, up 106% over a year earlier. This pace was even faster than the fiscal first quarter's 85% year-over-year growth. The data center business made up $89 billion of the total. And net income , at $59.7 billion, rose 126% year over year.\"] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'Revenue', 'period': 'fiscal 2027 second quarter (period ended July 26, 2026)', 'value': '$96.2 billion', 'kind': 'actual', 'basis': 'company total', 'party': 'Nvidia'}, {'n': 2, 'measure': 'Revenue growth year over year', 'period': 'fiscal 2027 second quarter', 'value': '106%', 'kind': 'actual', 'basis': None, 'party': 'Nvidia'}, {'n': 3, 'measure': 'Data center revenue', 'period': 'fiscal 2027 second quarter', 'value': '$89 billion', 'kind': 'actual', 'basis': 'data center business, of company total', 'party': 'Nvidia'}, {'n': 4, 'measure': 'Net income', 'period': 'fiscal 2027 second quarter', 'value': '$59.7 billion', 'kind': 'actual', 'basis': None, 'party': 'Nvidia'}] LINKS none\nSTATEMENT ev-2 PARTY Nvidia DATE None PASSAGES ['Guidance for the fiscal third quarter is $108 billion in revenue , around 12% above fiscal Q2.'] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'Revenue guidance', 'period': 'fiscal third quarter', 'value': '$108 billion', 'kind': 'guidance', 'basis': 'around 12% above fiscal Q2', 'party': 'Nvidia'}] LINKS none\nSTATEMENT ev-3 PARTY Nvidia DATE late August PASSAGES ['And on the company\\'s late-August earnings call, CFO Colette Kress said Nvidia expects revenue to rise roughly 70% in fiscal 2028, the year ending in January 2028. She called it \"a supply-constrained outlook.\" Put another way, the limit is manufacturing capacity, not customer demand.'] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'Revenue growth', 'period': 'fiscal 2028, the year ending in January 2028', 'value': 'roughly 70%', 'kind': 'guidance', 'basis': '\"a supply-constrained outlook\"', 'party': 'Nvidia (CFO Colette Kress)'}] LINKS [{'question': 'clean-2', 'new_question': False, 'reason': \"The CFO's statement that the fiscal 2028 outlook is constrained by manufacturing capacity rather than demand bears on whether Nvidia must lock in large purchase and supply commitments; the item gives no amount of such commitments, so it does not establish their size.\"}]\nSTATEMENT ev-4 PARTY Nvidia DATE late August PASSAGES [\"On the call, Kress said gross margins should bottom between 71% and 72% in the fiscal fourth quarter and then settle at 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as price hikes kick in. That'd be a drop from the fiscal second quarter's 75%, though a small one.\"] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'Gross margin', 'period': 'fiscal fourth quarter', 'value': 'between 71% and 72%', 'kind': 'guidance', 'basis': 'bottom level', 'party': 'Nvidia (CFO Colette Kress)'}, {'n': 2, 'measure': 'Gross margin', 'period': 'fiscal 2028', 'value': '72% to 73%', 'kind': 'guidance', 'basis': 'steady level as price hikes kick in', 'party': 'Nvidia (CFO Colette Kress)'}, {'n': 3, 'measure': 'Gross margin', 'period': 'fiscal second quarter', 'value': '75%', 'kind': 'actual', 'basis': None, 'party': 'Nvidia'}] LINKS none\nSTATEMENT ev-5 PARTY Analyst consensus DATE None PASSAGES [\"Analysts' consensus already has fiscal 2027 revenue coming in around $412 billion.\", \"Next to this fiscal year's expected 90% revenue growth and next year's forecast 70%, that would arguably be a low bar.\"] FIGURES [{'n': 1, 'measure': 'Revenue', 'period': 'fiscal 2027', 'value': 'around $412 billion', 'kind': 'estimate', 'basis': \"analysts' consensus\", 'party': 'consensus'}, {'n': 2, 'measure': 'Revenue growth', 'period': 'this fiscal year (fiscal 2027)', 'value': '90%', 'kind': 'estimate', 'basis': 'expected growth', 'party': 'consensus'}] LINKS none\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
