{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/figure-fields/reader-packet-1-settle.json\\\")); [print(a[\\\"article\\\"],a[\\\"publisher\\\"],a[\\\"publication_date\\\"]) for a in p[\\\"articles\\\"]]; [print(a[\\\"answer\\\"],[(s[\\\"id\\\"],s[\\\"summary\\\"]) for s in a[\\\"statements_with_figures\\\"]]) for a in p[\\\"answers\\\"] if a[\\\"answer\\\"] in (\\\"B19\\\",\\\"B21\\\",\\\"B07\\\",\\\"B10\\\")]'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/figure-fields/reader-packet-1-settle.json\\\")); [print(a[\\\"article\\\"],a[\\\"publisher\\\"],a[\\\"publication_date\\\"]) for a in p[\\\"articles\\\"]]; [print(a[\\\"answer\\\"],[(s[\\\"id\\\"],s[\\\"summary\\\"]) for s in a[\\\"statements_with_figures\\\"]]) for a in p[\\\"answers\\\"] if a[\\\"answer\\\"] in (\\\"B19\\\",\\\"B21\\\",\\\"B07\\\",\\\"B10\\\")]'\"","aggregated_output":"1 barchart.com 2026-09-22\n2 morningstar.com 2026-09-23\n3 zacks.com 2026-09-23\n6 finance.yahoo.com 2026-09-23\n7 trefis.com 2026-09-25\n8 fool.com 2026-09-25\nB07 [('e1', 'NVIDIA reported that fiscal second-quarter revenue more than doubled year over year to $96.2 billion, with data center revenue up 117% to $89 billion, as reported by Barchart.com.'), ('e2', 'NVIDIA management guided for approximately $108 billion in third-quarter revenue, which Barchart.com said implies 89% growth.'), ('e3', 'NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress guided for 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028, far exceeding the 45% growth Wall Street had previously modeled, according to Barchart.com.'), ('e5', \"Barchart.com estimated that roughly 25% of NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 revenue is expected to come from customers receiving some form of company-backed financing, potentially $175 billion funded off NVIDIA's own balance sheet.\"), ('e6', \"Barchart.com reported that NVIDIA's off-balance-sheet guarantees exceed $100 billion, tied to projects such as the SB Energy campus for OpenAI.\"), ('e7', \"Barchart.com reported that analysts' earnings estimates for NVIDIA were revised sharply higher over the past nine months, from $8.50 to $15.68 per share for fiscal 2029.\")]\nB10 [('ev-1', \"NVIDIA's fiscal second-quarter revenue more than doubled year over year to $96.2 billion, with data center revenue up 117% to $89 billion, as reported in the article.\"), ('ev-2', 'NVIDIA management guided third-quarter revenue to approximately $108 billion, implying 89% growth, per the article.'), ('ev-3', 'NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress guided for 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028, far above the 45% growth Wall Street had previously modeled, according to the article.'), ('ev-5', \"The article states NVIDIA is financing a growing share of its sales to AI startups, with roughly 25% of fiscal 2028 revenue expected to come from customers receiving some form of company-backed financing, potentially $175 billion funded off NVIDIA's own balance sheet.\"), ('ev-6', 'The article states NVIDIA carries off-balance-sheet guarantees exceeding $100 billion tied to projects such as the SB Energy campus for OpenAI, which it says introduce credit risk not captured by traditional valuation metrics.'), ('ev-7', 'The article reports that consensus earnings estimates for NVIDIA have been revised sharply higher over just the past nine months, from $8.50 to $15.68 per share for fiscal 2029.')]\nB19 [('ev-1', \"NVIDIA reported fiscal 2027 second-quarter revenue of $96.22 billion, up 105.85% year over year, with non-GAAP EPS of $2.22 beating consensus by 6.29%, and Data Center revenue of $89.023 billion, as recounted in 24/7 Wall St.'s 23 September 2026 article.\"), ('ev-2', 'NVIDIA guided fiscal 2027 third-quarter revenue to $108 billion, and the article states that this Q3 guidance excludes China Data Center compute revenue, citing geopolitical uncertainty.'), ('ev-3', \"The article states NVIDIA's gross margins are expected to bottom in the 71% to 72% range in Q4 on memory cost inflation, recovering to 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as volumes scale.\"), ('ev-4', \"24/7 Wall St. lists what it calls NVIDIA's real risks as supply commitments of $279 billion, guarantee obligations capped at $108.5 billion, and days sales outstanding extending to 60 days.\"), ('ev-5', 'NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang told investors that NVIDIA can supply only 70% of demand, with fiscal 2028 growth pegged at approximately 70%, according to the article.')]\nB21 [('ev-1', 'NVIDIA reported data center revenue of $89 billion in fiscal Q2 2027 out of $96 billion in total revenue, and management guided fiscal Q3 2027 revenue to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, a midpoint the Trefis article calculates as about 12% above the Q2 total.'), ('ev-3', 'NVIDIA said memory prices rose more than it expected and it reset its margin expectations, guiding gross margin to 74% for fiscal Q3 2027, down from 75% in Q2, and expecting gross margin to bottom at 71% to 72% in fiscal Q4.'), ('ev-4', \"NVIDIA has invested nearly $50 billion in AI labs, and management expects AI labs backed by NVIDIA's balance sheet to make up roughly a quarter of NVIDIA's business in fiscal 2028 — a portion of its business resting on customers NVIDIA helps fund.\"), ('ev-5', \"Trefis calculated that NVIDIA's revenue grew 83% over the past year, against 16.7% for Texas Instruments, and that NVIDIA kept 65.2 cents of each sales dollar as operating profit, against 38.1 cents at TI.\")]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
